---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import VideoFigure from '../components/VideoFigure.astro';
import teamFlag from '../assets/njord-team-flag.jpg';
import popUpLights from '../assets/njord-pop-up-lights.jpg';

const scoreboard = [
  { label: 'Opening round', value: '4th' },
  { label: 'Final standing', value: '14th' },
  { label: 'Lost for good', value: 'Lidars, BMS' },
];

// All clips were filmed on the final day of the competition, once the boat had
// been rebuilt. Sizes match the encoded files in /public/videos.
const onWater = [
  {
    name: 'smooth-driving',
    title: 'Driving under power',
    duration: '0:13',
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    caption: 'The boat running on open water on the last day of the competition.',
  },
  {
    name: 'ama-height-live',
    title: 'Setting ride height live',
    duration: '0:25',
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    caption:
      'The amas driving up and down to set the height of the boat in the water, adjusted live while under way.',
  },
  {
    name: 'ama-retract-on-water',
    title: 'Amas retracting on water',
    duration: '0:04',
    width: 1280,
    height: 736,
    caption: 'A short look at the amas pulling back in while the boat is floating.',
  },
];

const onBench = [
  {
    name: 'tilt-only',
    title: 'Roll axis only',
    duration: '0:14',
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    caption: 'The amas alone, driving up and down to fight roll.',
  },
  {
    name: 'pitch-only',
    title: 'Pitch axis only',
    duration: '0:07',
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    caption: 'The battery alone, sliding forward and back along its rails to trim pitch.',
  },
  {
    name: 'battery-dry-test',
    title: 'Battery travel, end to end',
    duration: '0:13',
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    caption:
      'The battery running from full forward to full aft and back again, showing the complete range of the pitch-trim slider.',
  },
  {
    name: 'ama-height-dry-test',
    title: 'Ama travel, end to end',
    duration: '0:16',
    width: 1280,
    height: 720,
    caption: 'Both amas extending and retracting through their full stroke on the bench.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Njord 2026 — Ligmax | Fourth after round one, fourteenth overall"
  description="How Ligmax's first Njord Autonomous Ship Challenge went: a flooded boat on day one, fourth place in the opening round, and a part-by-part rebuild filmed on the final day."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="page-intro">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="intro-eyebrow">Njord 2026 &middot; Trondheim</span>
        <h1>Fourth after round one, fourteenth by the end</h1>
        <p>
          The tasks were not what beat us. Hardware was. On the first day of testing the boat went under,
          and although we got it running again in time to place fourth in the opening round, the damage
          kept surfacing for the rest of the week. This is what happened, and what the boat could still do
          on the final day.
        </p>
        <ul class="scoreboard">
          {scoreboard.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <span class="scoreboard-value">{item.value}</span>
              <span class="scoreboard-label">{item.label}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="story" data-reveal>
          <h2>The boat went under during testing</h2>
          <p>
            On our first day of testing the Pixhawk lost its settings. The main thrusters were no longer
            configured as bidirectional, so the moment we armed the boat they went to full reverse. The
            boat was pulled under, and everything on board went with it.
          </p>
          <p>
            We saved it from sinking, but it came out full of water. We took every part out, cleaned all of
            it, and flushed everything with fresh water three times in a row to get the seawater out, with a
            lot of electronic cleaner on top. Most of it came back. The lidars did not — those were the one
            thing that died permanently that day.
          </p>
          <p>
            That loss mattered more than any other. Both 360° lidars are what give Ligmax range data on
            every bearing, and the whole obstacle-detection chain — clustering scan returns into buoys,
            then colouring them from the cameras — starts there. The gimbal we built to hold the bow lidar
            level survived; the sensor it was built for did not.
          </p>

          <h2>Fourth place, one day later</h2>
          <p>
            We went out the next day and placed fourth in the opening round. That was the high point of the
            week, and it happened roughly twenty-four hours after pulling a flooded boat out of the
            fjord.
          </p>

          <h2>Then it came apart, one piece at a time</h2>
          <p>
            The cleaning bought us the opening round, but it did not stop what the seawater had started.
            Oxidation kept spreading, and components failed one after another for the rest of the
            competition. We finished fourteenth overall. The tasks themselves were not as hard as we had
            expected going in — we simply could not keep the hardware alive long enough to run them.
          </p>

          <h2>Rebuilt by the final day</h2>
          <p>
            We clawed it back part by part, and by the last day of the competition the boat was close to
            full function again. Only the lidars and the battery management system stayed dead. Every video
            below was filmed that day.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--soft">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="clips-head" data-reveal>
          <span class="eyebrow">Final day &middot; On the water</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">What it could still do</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">
            Filmed after the rebuild, running on the fjord without lidars or the BMS.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="clip-grid clip-grid--three">
          {onWater.map((clip) => <VideoFigure {...clip} />)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="clips-head" data-reveal>
          <span class="eyebrow">Final day &middot; On the bench</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">The stabilisation system, moving</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">
            Ligmax trims itself on two axes: the amas drive up and down against roll, and the battery
            slides fore and aft against pitch. On the bench you can watch both react to the hull being
            tipped by hand.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="clip-feature">
          <VideoFigure
            name="tilt-and-roll-dry-test"
            title="Both axes together"
            duration="0:49"
            width={1280}
            height={720}
            caption="The hull rolled and pitched by hand on the table. The battery slides forward and back and the amas drive up and down in response — the same corrections that would hold the boat level in the water."
            featured
          />
        </div>

        <div class="clip-grid clip-grid--two">
          {onBench.map((clip) => <VideoFigure {...clip} />)}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--soft">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="aftermath" data-reveal>
          <div class="aftermath-text">
            <span class="eyebrow">Aftermath</span>
            <h2 class="section-title">Still emptying it out</h2>
            <p>
              Water stayed in the boat long after the day it went under. This is us draining the NEMA
              enclosure in the bottom of the bow — one of the places seawater sat and kept working on the
              electronics all week.
            </p>
          </div>
          <VideoFigure
            name="nema-water"
            title="Draining the bow NEMA"
            duration="0:03"
            width={1280}
            height={932}
            caption="Emptying the NEMA enclosure at the bottom front of the boat."
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="stills">
          <figure class="still" data-reveal>
            <Image
              src={popUpLights}
              alt="The forward-facing pop-up lights on the Ligmax hull opened and lit inside the workshop"
              widths={[560, 860, 1200]}
              sizes="(max-width: 860px) 92vw, 540px"
            />
            <figcaption>
              The forward-facing lights popped open and lit. They survived the flooding.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="still" data-reveal>
            <Image
              src={teamFlag}
              alt="Two Ligmax team members holding a Norwegian flag behind the vessel at the Njord 2026 competition site"
              widths={[560, 860, 1200]}
              sizes="(max-width: 860px) 92vw, 540px"
            />
            <figcaption>Ligmax and the boat at the Njord 2026 site in Trondheim.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="next-year" data-reveal>
          <h2>What we take into next year</h2>
          <p>
            We came away knowing the tasks are within reach — we were never short on capability, we were
            short on hardware that survived the week. Waterproofing, connector choice and a recovery plan
            for a flooded boat are now the first things on the list rather than the last. We learned a
            great deal this year, and we are going back with high expectations.
          </p>
          <div class="next-year-actions">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/docs/ligmax-technical-report-2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              Read the technical report (PDF)
            </a>
            <a class="btn btn--outline" href="/#contact">Partner with us</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-intro {
    background:
      radial-gradient(44rem 20rem at 78% 0%, rgba(79, 127, 206, 0.16), transparent 62%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--navy-950), var(--navy-800));
    color: #c3cee6;
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .intro-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #9db8e8;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }

  .page-intro h1 {
    color: #fff;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .page-intro p {
    max-width: 68ch;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .scoreboard {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
  }

  .scoreboard-value {
    display: block;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .scoreboard-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #9db8e8;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
  }

  .story {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .story h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 1.7rem);
    margin-top: 2.2rem;
  }

  .story h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .story p {
    font-size: 1.04rem;
  }

  .clips-head {
    margin-bottom: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.6rem);
  }

  .clip-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .clip-grid--three {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }

  .clip-grid--two {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .clip-feature {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .aftermath {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .aftermath-text p {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .stills {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .still {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .still img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .still figcaption {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .next-year {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .next-year p {
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  .next-year-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .clip-grid--three {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .clip-grid--three,
    .clip-grid--two,
    .aftermath,
    .stills {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .scoreboard {
      gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
